.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH stint 1  "stint 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
stint \- Time tracker that syncs with Solidtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstint\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Time tracker that syncs with Solidtime
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON instead of human text
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
stint\-start(1)
Start a new timer
.TP
stint\-stop(1)
Stop the running timer
.TP
stint\-current(1)
Show the currently running timer (or none)
.TP
stint\-restart(1)
Start a new timer using an existing entry\*(Aqs description/project/billable
.TP
stint\-today(1)
Show today\*(Aqs entries
.TP
stint\-list(1)
List entries between two dates
.TP
stint\-edit(1)
Edit an entry
.TP
stint\-delete(1)
Delete an entry
.TP
stint\-config(1)
View and modify configuration
.TP
stint\-projects(1)
Refresh and list projects/tasks/tags
.TP
stint\-sync(1)
Sync queue commands (drain, retry\-abandoned)
.TP
stint\-pull(1)
Pull running\-timer and recent state from Solidtime
.TP
stint\-calendar(1)
Connect, list, and manage calendar accounts
.TP
stint\-api(1)
Inspect the loopback HTTP API (bind address, port)
.TP
stint\-mcp(1)
Run as an MCP server on stdio (for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, …)
.TP
stint\-skill(1)
Install / uninstall the stint MCP server + skill in editor harnesses
.TP
stint\-generate\-man(1)
Generate the stint(1) man page into the given directory
.TP
stint\-update(1)
Check for and apply updates to the standalone CLI. No\-op for .app\-bundled installs
.TP
stint\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
